PICADS LICENSE

PICADS — Procedural Integrated Circuit Architecture and Design System
Original and principal creator: MotionflowOffical
Official source code: https://github.com/MotionflowOffical/PICADS

Copyright (c) 2026 MotionflowOffical for original material actually owned by
that author. Other authors retain copyright in their respective contributions.

This License permits private and commercial use of PICADS, including commercial
sale of independently produced chips and designs, subject to the mandatory
PICADS attribution in Section 7. It permits no-charge sharing of PICADS code
with matching source. Standalone sale, resale, or paywalling of PICADS code or
software access is prohibited without the actual copyright holder's written
permission. A genuinely broader paid product may include PICADS if it meets
ALL conditions of the Paid Integration Exception in Section 3, including free,
independent public access to the exact corresponding PICADS source. Private
modifications used solely in an internal engineering workflow need not be
published. The requirements of this License apply only to rights that the
relevant licensor actually controls.

1. DEFINITIONS

"PICADS" means the original program and materials lawfully offered under this
License by the rights holder(s). A "Covered Work" means PICADS software,
software copying copyright-protected PICADS material, and modifications or
copyright derivatives of that software, but only to the extent the applicable
rights holder is legally able to license the material. Calling something a
fork, plugin, wrapper, adaptation or differently branded application does not
by itself change whether PICADS code has been copied or modified.

A "PICADS Component" is the portion of a combined product or service that is a
Covered Work, together with modifications and components necessary to build,
run and modify that portion. An independent application that merely invokes
PICADS through a documented process, command-line or network interface does
not automatically become a Covered Work merely by interacting with it. A
substantive change to PICADS itself remains a Covered Work even if embedded in
an otherwise independent application.

"Corresponding Source" is the complete, preferred, human-readable source for
the exact PICADS Component released or deployed, including all modifications,
patches, relevant interfaces/adapters that are themselves Covered Works,
generation inputs, build and installation scripts, configurations and clear
instructions to reproduce that PICADS Component. It excludes independently
created, separable host-application code not containing PICADS-protected
material, generally available tools and independent third-party libraries;
the latter must be identified so the component can be built using lawfully
available equivalents. Source which requires a paid proprietary host, key or
secret just to build or run the PICADS Component on its own does not satisfy
this definition unless a complete publicly usable replacement for that
requirement is included. Removing confidential credentials from examples is
allowed; concealing functional PICADS modifications is not.

"Distribution" means providing the Covered Work or copies of its source or
binaries to someone else, including through download, shipment, publishing,
resale or bundling. "Network Deployment" means allowing third parties to
operate or invoke functions of a PICADS Component over a network, even if no
copy is transferred. A contractor operating the software only within a
customer's confidential project and delivering independent results is not,
solely for that reason, providing the customer with Network Deployment.

"Commercial Use" means professional, business, research-for-profit or other
revenue-related use of PICADS, including privately modified copies, that does
not necessarily involve Distribution or Network Deployment. "Independent
Outputs" means chips, GDS/layout files, designs, masks, engineering reports,
and other independently usable outputs produced using PICADS. Outputs do not
become Covered Works solely because PICADS helped create them, but embedded
copies of PICADS source remain Covered Works.

A "Paid Integration" is Distribution of or Network Deployment involving a
PICADS Component within a broader, paid product or hosted application that
also provides material independently implemented functionality. "Standalone
PICADS Monetization" means charging for PICADS code, copies or access as the
primary or materially equivalent offering, including cosmetic repackaging,
resale, a minimally altered fork, or a thin paywalled wrapper whose primary
function is to provide PICADS functionality. Payment to a different company
or intermediary, a new name, UI restyling, hosting, or a token extra feature
does not turn Standalone PICADS Monetization into a Paid Integration.

"Previously Free Public Edition" means PICADS code or an edition of PICADS
that was in fact made available to the public without charge and with the
applicable source access. Availability is determined by the code actually
published, not by a version number, marketing name, repository ownership,
announced future availability, or a claim that a copy is a new edition.
An "Author-Unpublished Edition" means a distinct edition prepared or
expressly authorized by the actual PICADS Author that has not previously
been made publicly available for free in that edition. A third party cannot
create an Author-Unpublished Edition by renaming, packaging, modifying,
or republishing freely available PICADS code; actual authorship and rights
control, not attribution text, determine who may separately license it.

"PICADS Author" means the actual copyright owner of the original PICADS code
publicly credited as MotionflowOffical, not anyone who merely claims that
account name or prints the creator credit. "Official Source Repository" is
https://github.com/MotionflowOffical/PICADS. Links to forks, mirrors,
profiles or shortened URLs do not replace that original-credit link.

2. USE, PRIVATE MODIFICATIONS, INDEPENDENT OUTPUTS AND FREE SHARING

Subject to this License and any independent third-party rights, an authorized
recipient may use, study, copy, run, and modify PICADS privately, including
in commercial engineering and to produce and sell Independent Outputs. No
PICADS software royalty is charged merely for selling chips or other
Independent Outputs, but commercial attribution under Section 7 is required.
Private PICADS modifications need not be disclosed merely because they were
used to generate commercially sold outputs. This permission does not include
selling access to the PICADS software itself.

A recipient may distribute Covered Works at no charge if they concurrently
make exact Corresponding Source freely available under this License and
comply with the license, notice, naming, change-identification and WIP rules.
Distribution or deployment inside a genuinely broader paid application is
additionally possible ONLY under the Section 3 Paid Integration Exception.

3. STANDALONE RESELLING PROHIBITED; PAID INTEGRATION EXCEPTION

3.1. Except where the PICADS Author and all other necessary rights holders
have granted an explicit, verifiable written exception under Section 4, no
recipient may engage in Standalone PICADS Monetization. In particular, no
recipient may sell copies of PICADS, sell PICADS source, charge to download,
install, activate or use PICADS as a standalone program, resell an ordinary
fork, paywall the exact PICADS software, or sell a hosted instance of PICADS
with no independently substantial broader product. A charge renamed a
"donation," "support fee," "access fee," "consulting subscription," or
"deployment fee" does not evade this rule when access to PICADS itself is
conditional on payment.

3.2. A third party MAY include a PICADS Component within a paid desktop
application, EDA suite, device package, engineering platform, or hosted
product, without a special paid-distribution grant, ONLY when ALL conditions
below are met:

(a) The broader offering has material, genuinely independent functionality
    separate from PICADS. Rebranding, trivial UI layers, installation scripts,
    minor format conversion, a launcher, an access gateway, or token add-ons
    do not alone qualify. It must be useful for substantive reasons other
    than obtaining a paid copy of, or remote access to, PICADS.

(b) The exact Corresponding Source for the PICADS Component actually shipped
    or deployed, including every change made to PICADS, is published at a
    conspicuous, stable HTTPS download URL accessible to ALL persons at no
    charge, without purchase, subscription, payment details, paid account,
    mandatory registration, or special permission. It must be available no
    later than the start of paid distribution/deployment and remain freely
    available while that version is offered or supported AND for at least
    three years after the last paid distribution or deployment of that
    version. A change of owner, reseller, service provider or domain does
    not shorten that obligation. Users must be able to retain and build the
    downloaded PICADS source independently of the paid host application.

(c) The paid offering and every relevant download, About/credits or
    documentation entry must clearly identify the PICADS Component, provide
    the free exact-version source URL, include the official PICADS origin URL
    and original creator credit, and disclose changes to PICADS. A generic
    link to the original unmodified project does NOT replace the exact
    modified source URL. The host application may have its own primary name,
    but the embedded PICADS Component must be clearly identified as PICADS.

(d) The PICADS Component and exact Corresponding Source must remain under
    this License and remain freely shareable under Section 2. No EULA,
    DRM, activation scheme, contract, license key, conflicting IP term,
    technical measure or third-party agreement may remove those rights or
    require paid access to the PICADS Component as separately buildable code.
    Terms for genuinely independent host-application code may differ.

(e) The inclusion must not falsely imply authorization or endorsement by the
    PICADS Author; no distributor obtains the author's exclusive rights or
    a standalone PICADS resale license merely by complying with this
    exception. Contractors, vendors and downstream redistributors must
    preserve these same conditions for every copy they provide.

3.3. Examples (these illustrate the conditions; labels cannot override them):

    PERMITTED: A paid CAD suite provides original schematic, analysis and
    collaboration features plus a PICADS backend, and publishes the exact
    modified PICADS backend source freely under Sections 3.2 and 5.

    PERMITTED: A paid hosted design platform provides independently valuable
    design-management and analysis tools and embeds PICADS execution, while
    offering the deployed PICADS Component's exact source freely and meeting
    Sections 3.2 and 5. Private designs and separable host code stay private.

    PERMITTED: An engineering consultancy uses a privately modified PICADS
    installation internally to deliver chips, files or reports. Customers
    receive only Independent Outputs, not access to PICADS software. There
    is no source-publication trigger solely for this internal use; Section 7
    attribution still applies.

    PROHIBITED: An identical PICADS download sold for money or a PICADS API
    placed behind a paywall, even if an unchanged upstream source URL is
    displayed. A renamed PICADS with a new launcher, cosmetics or a token
    feature remains prohibited Standalone PICADS Monetization.

3.4. Source publication under this exception is not permission to charge
separately for PICADS. If the PICADS Component is independently distributed,
that distribution must comply with Section 2. Where it is not clear whether
a paid product has substantial independent functionality, the recipient
must obtain Section 4 permission before relying on the Paid Integration
Exception; a mere claim of integration does not satisfy Section 3.2.

4. RIGHTS-HOLDER AUTHORIZATION, ORIGINAL AUTHOR AND CONTRIBUTIONS

Only the actual rightsholder can grant exceptions for rights they own or
control. Written commercial permissions outside Section 3.2 must identify
the granting actual owner, recipient, versions/code, permitted conduct, term
and any separately necessary contributors' permissions. Merely putting the
project in MotionflowOffical's name, using the PICADS brand, being a
contributor or preserving credit does not make a fork the original author's
release and does not grant Standalone PICADS Monetization rights.

A Previously Free Public Edition remains available under the free permissions
that applied when its code was made publicly available. Recipients may
continue to use, study, modify and redistribute that edition without charge
subject to this License; a later decision by the PICADS Author to offer a
separate paid edition does not withdraw or convert those existing rights.
The creator is not required by this paragraph to maintain a particular
website forever; a discontinued download does not terminate rights already
granted to lawful recipients.

The actual PICADS Author may separately offer an Author-Unpublished Edition
under different terms, including paid terms, only to the extent the author
owns or holds the required permission for its contents. That permission
concerns the distinct author-controlled edition, not copies of previously
free public code already licensed to recipients. An edition cannot be
reclassified as never-public solely by changing its name, wrapper, build
number, hosting location or method of distribution. Attribution to the
original creator does not make a third-party fork an author-owned edition.

Contributors retain their copyrights unless separately transferred. The
PICADS Author cannot issue additional commercial licenses for someone
else's independent contribution without sufficient rights. Contributions
accepted into the official PICADS project are subject to the separately signed
Contributor License Agreement (CLA) policy described in CONTRIBUTING.md and
`docs/CONTRIBUTOR_AGREEMENT.md`, granting the PICADS Author a nonexclusive
right to relicense those accepted contributions, including for distinct
author-controlled editions not previously made publicly available for free.
A proposed or unsigned CLA grants no rights; third-party
fork contributions do not become covered by an official-project CLA merely
because they exist. Contributors are responsible for authorized third-party
content and employer permissions. Existing external contributions and
dependencies require independent rights review.

5. EXACT SOURCE DISCLOSURE; NETWORK DEPLOYMENT; PRIVATE WORK

For every no-charge Distribution and every Paid Integration under Section 3.2,
the PICADS Component's actual Corresponding Source must be available to all
recipients, with the exact version/commit identifier, build instructions and
complete modifications. A clear download on the relevant distribution page
or documentation is acceptable if not gated by payment or registration.
For qualifying Network Deployment of a modified Covered Work to outsiders,
including a freely accessible PICADS web application or a permitted paid
integration, its operator must provide the same source access while the
service is provided. Section 3.2 sets the additional retention period for
paid integrations.

Use of PICADS inside an organization or by a contractor solely to deliver
Independent Outputs does not trigger release of private modifications, even
if the work is paid. Neither the code of a genuinely independent paid host
application nor private chip designs, netlists, customer files, internal
workflows, secrets and independent reports become mandatory public source
merely because they interface with PICADS. Copying PICADS-owned code into a
nominally independent module does not create such an exemption. The Official
Source Repository link is for origin attribution and NEVER replaces the
matching modified-source download required when source disclosure applies.

6. PERMANENT PROJECT NAME, AUTHORSHIP AND MODIFICATION NOTICE

Distributed Covered Works must retain PICADS as the name of the Covered Work
and the PICADS Component (including within any paid host). Forks may add a
qualifier such as "PICADS — Community Fork" but must not erase the original
name. Paid host applications may retain their own independent product names
if the PICADS Component is clearly identified within them. Every distribution
must prominently preserve this notice in its README/NOTICE and About or
credits (or CLI --about/help for CLI-only software):

  PICADS — Procedural Integrated Circuit Architecture and Design System.
  Original and principal creator: MotionflowOffical.
  Official PICADS source code: https://github.com/MotionflowOffical/PICADS

Clearly credit additional authors of their own changes, identify the fork or
integration maintainer, provide a meaningful change notice and avoid any
false claim of original authorship or official endorsement. An attribution
notice grants no exceptions to Section 3.

7. MANDATORY COMMERCIAL ATTRIBUTION AND SUFFICIENT INTERNAL RECORDS

Every Commercial Use, including commercial use of privately modified copies,
requires this original-creator attribution and link to the official source:

  Made using PICADS — Procedural Integrated Circuit Architecture and Design
  System. Original and principal creator: MotionflowOffical.
  Official PICADS source code: https://github.com/MotionflowOffical/PICADS

Publicly marketed products or customer-facing Independent Outputs must show
this notice in relevant product documentation, user guide, project report,
client handoff or product listing, associated with the actual product; a
physical chip need not be marked. Digital links must be directly clickable;
printed URLs must be legible. Confidential client work may carry the notice
privately in delivered documentation without publishing customer designs.
A fork URL, generic logo, buried unrelated legal page or merely the
original author's profile is not a substitute.

For exclusively internal Commercial Use with no external deliverable, one
accessible, durable record per applicable project, product family or toolchain
is sufficient; a separate notice for every run, generated file or chip is NOT
required. An internal project README, design-system inventory, compliance
record, build manifest or engineering wiki page qualifies if it contains the
complete notice above, identifies which project/toolchain uses PICADS, and
records the PICADS version or commit when known. An organization using
contractors, subsidiaries or automated build systems may centralize this
record, provided the relevant teams can locate it. Retain the internal record
while the use continues and for at least three years after the last
Commercial Use of the associated project or toolchain. If records are
reasonably requested to resolve a specific attribution dispute, confirmation
may be limited to the relevant notice and version without disclosing customer
secrets or other proprietary files, subject to applicable law. There is no
general audit or unrestricted access right created by this clause.

Every entity that uses PICADS commercially is responsible for its own
applicable notice, but may satisfy the requirement through an accessible
shared project record or correctly attributed client deliverable when that
record covers its role. Neither subcontracting nor white-labeling is an
excuse to remove author credit. Attribution alone never grants rights to
sell or paywall the PICADS Component. Attribution alone never triggers
publication of privately modified code.

8. THIRD-PARTY RIGHTS; WIP WARNINGS

No PICADS copyright permission covers unrelated tools, process-design
kits, cells, models, dependencies, libraries, data or code of third parties
without their permission. Distributors must comply with independent licenses
on such material. Preserve LICENSE, NOTICE and a clear WIP warning, including
references to docs/KNOWN_ISSUES_AND_LIMITATIONS.md or an equally accessible
version of the project's then-current known limitations. PICADS is
experimental; a generated GDS does not establish manufacturing signoff.

