AND RIGHTS HOLDERS ARE NOT LIABLE FOR LOSSES ARISING FROM USE OR FABRICATION.
MANDATORY STATUTORY RIGHTS AND LIABILITY RULES PREVAIL.

10. COMPLIANCE; CURE; SEVERABILITY; PREVIOUSLY FREE PUBLIC CODE

Rights granted to a noncompliant recipient terminate for a knowing material
breach, including hidden paid PICADS resale, suppression of required source,
or failure to provide required commercial attribution. Rights are reinstated
provisionally upon stopping and curing the breach, and permanently if the
relevant holder gives no notice within 60 days after cure or if a first
notified breach is cured within 30 days of receipt of notice. This cure
provision does not authorize continued distribution without the required
source. Lawfully received rights of compliant downstream recipients are not
terminated by another person's breach.

If any provision is unenforceable, the remainder applies to the extent
permitted by law; no severability rule creates an otherwise forbidden right
to sell PICADS. Permissions for PICADS editions that were actually made
publicly available
free of charge are not retroactively withdrawn by a later paid, separately
licensed or unpublished author-controlled edition. Earlier lawfully obtained
free copies retain the permissions under which they were received. Rights
in contributions and external code remain with their actual owners unless
duly transferred or licensed.
